Z||000000||Manta||12-24-2000||06:42 PM||||Every time I wash my 86 ½ 6 cyl, The speedometer will work for about 4 – 5 miles.<BR>I know why this happens ( The water is a conductor ) but I don’t know where.<BR>Does anyone know where the wires go after leaving the sensor?<BR>Do they come up on the battery side? The air filter side?<BR>Or in the middle under the rear window?<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||12-24-2000||08:33 PM||||In the middle. It is included within the engine harness.<BR>Is this the only time it works?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Manta||12-25-2000||02:16 AM||||Yes, I was just getting ready to buy a new sensor when I washed it and it started working. Then I went back and just sprayed the hose on the back end and drove it and again it worked for a couple of miles then stopped.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||12-25-2000||05:20 AM||||Sounds like you should check the condition of the pig tail from the sensor to the main area of the harness. May just be a bad plug. Is this the first time it has worked for you (after washing)? Then again, it may have been a fluke and the connections at the instrument cluster may need cleaned.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Manta||12-25-2000||12:03 PM||||I usually don’t drive it after washing it.<BR>But now I have sprayed it about ten times<BR>trying to narrow it down.<BR>It is defiantly a wire in the back. <BR>||||reg||1
